    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0584" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg370"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 156.</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr. Bancroft</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 16, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bancroft:</hi></p>
                <p>Washburne complains that his dispatches are detained two to three <pb facs="0585"
                        n="371" xml:id="pg371"/> weeks between London and Paris. This is a poor
                    return for his services in behalf of Germans, many hundreds of whom he is
                    protecting and feeding in Paris. Endeavor to have this wrong remedied. We are
                    entitled to prompt communication with our minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
